let __v_314 = Value::from("It is not one-sided. The operation is a general anaesthetic, which is very safe in a healthy young animal but is the one real risk, and in a large or giant breed neutering before the growth plates close is linked to joint trouble later, which is why many people wait until a year or more. What waiting takes on is everything the operation removes: pyometra, a womb infection that needs an emergency operation, and mammary tumours in a female; and the roaming, marking and fights in a male. Ask your vet about the timing for your animal - most will talk the trade-off through rather than push a date.");
