let __v_449 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"rabbit\",\"Spot-clean the wet corner and the litter tray every day, change the bedding once a week and give the hutch a deep clean once a month: rabbit urine soaks into wood and the ammonia it gives off damages their lungs. Use a pet-safe disinfectant or a 1:10 white vinegar solution, rinse and dry it before the rabbit goes back in, and skip the phenolic ones like Jeyes fluid - they are toxic to small animals. Vinegar is also what takes the chalky white urine marks off the floor.\"],[\"guinea pig\",\"Spot-clean the wet corner and the litter tray every day, change the bedding once a week and give the cage a deep clean once a month: guinea-pig urine soaks into wood and the ammonia it gives off damages their lungs. Use a pet-safe disinfectant or a 1:10 white vinegar solution, rinse and dry it before the guinea pigs go back in, and skip phenolic ones like Jeyes fluid. Keep a handful of the old bedding to put back, because a cage that smells completely new makes them nervous.\"],[\"hamster\",\"Spot-clean the wet corner every day and change the bedding every few weeks, with a full scrub of the cage once a month: hamster urine is concentrated and the ammonia builds up fast in a small cage. Hot soapy water or a pet-safe cleaner, rinsed and dried right through before the bedding goes back, because a damp cage gives a hamster a chill and a chest infection. Put a handful of the old bedding back in the nest so the cage still smells of home.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("_PET_CLEANING", __v_449.clone())?;
