let __v_827 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"bone\",\"cooked bones splinter and a splinter is a vet job, so give a proper chew instead of anything off the plate. A small bit of gristle is not a problem.\"],[\"sausage\",\"sausages are salty and fatty: a piece is fine, a plateful is a bad habit.\"],[\"bacon\",\"bacon is salty and fatty: a piece is fine, a plateful is a bad habit.\"],[\"ham\",\"ham is salty and fatty: a piece is fine, a plateful is a bad habit.\"],[\"chips\",\"chips are fat and salt: one is a treat, a handful is a bad idea.\"],[\"salt\",\"salt is dangerous in quantity and {one}'s portion is tiny, so keep it out of reach. If a lot has gone down, ring the vet: too much salt is an emergency.\"],[\"sugar\",\"sugar is just empty calories, and it is the sugar-free sort with xylitol in it that is the dangerous one.\"],[\"avocado\",\"the flesh is not a poison to a dog or a cat, but the stone is a blockage and the skin is hard to digest, so a bit of flesh is fine and the stone has to be out of reach. It is birds it kills.\"],[\"ice cream\",\"a lick of plain vanilla does no harm, and the dairy, the sugar and the chocolate sort are the three reasons not to give a bowl of it.\"],[\"pizza\",\"salt, fat, and often onion or garlic, which damage a dog's red cells: a corner is not an emergency, and a slice is the vet if it is a small dog.\"],[\"raw egg\",\"a raw egg is not a poison, but the white is hard to digest and salmonella is the reason to cook it: a cooked or scrambled egg is the better treat.\"],[\"coffee\",\"caffeine is a poison to dogs and cats, and it is a vet call: keep cups and coffee grounds and caffeine tablets out of reach, and say how much went down.\"],[\"macadamia\",\"macadamia nuts are a poison to dogs even in small numbers: ring the vet and say how many, and do not wait for the wobble to start.\"],[\"burnt\",\"burnt toast or bread is not worth giving: scrape the black off, or use a fresh slice, because the charred part is not food. Plain toast is otherwise just bread.\"]]}")?;
