let __v_1575 = Value::from("A cat and a child get on fine with three rules: never leave a baby or a toddler alone in a room with the cat, give the cat somewhere up high and a room it can leave by, and show the child one finger down the back and to leave the cat alone while it is eating or in its basket. The old story that a cat smothers a baby is not true - a cat goes to warmth, so keep it out of the cot, and shut the bedroom and the pram against it while the baby sleeps. A swat is nearly always fear rather than nastiness: a cat that swats a child it used to accept should see the vet, because pain is often behind a change. Wash any scratch with soap and water, and a deep bite on a hand wants looking at.");
