let __v_1624 = Value::from("A cat is the cheaper of the two to keep: about 800 to 1,200 pounds a year against 1,000 to 1,700 for a dog, because insurance is 8 to 20 a month instead of 20 to 40 and a cat eats far less than a medium dog. The buying price is the other way round - a pedigree puppy is usually dearer than a pedigree kitten - but over ten years the dog costs the most.");
