let __v_1920 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"rabbit\",\"Hay and water are the whole job now: leave both within reach and watch the droppings. A bit of bread, fruit or something off a plate is usually fine, but a rabbit's gut has to keep moving - soft or no droppings within twelve hours, or a rabbit that sits hunched and will not eat, is the vet today. Do not starve it and do not wait for it to pick up, because a rabbit that stops eating goes downhill inside a day.\"],[\"guinea pig\",\"Hay, water and the nuggets are the whole job now, and watch the droppings. A bit of something off a plate is usually fine, but a guinea pig's gut has to keep moving - soft or no droppings within twelve hours, or one that sits hunched and will not eat, is the vet today. It cannot make its own vitamin C, so do not let a plate of scraps replace the nuggets.\"],[\"hamster\",\"Clear out what is left and keep its own food and water going, and watch it: a hamster that is still busy, eating and hoarding is fine, because a scrap of most human food is a treat rather than a poison. The trouble is what a mixed plate carries - salt, sugar, cheese and fried food - so expect a loose back end, and ring the vet if it is hunched, cold, not eating or has diarrhoea for more than a day.\"],[\"gerbil\",\"Clear out what is left and keep its own food and water going, and watch it: a gerbil that is still busy, eating and digging is fine, because a scrap of most human food is a treat rather than a poison. Salt, sugar and fried food are what a mixed plate carries, so expect a loose back end, and ring the vet if it is hunched, cold, not eating or loose for more than a day.\"],[\"chinchilla\",\"Clear out what is left and keep the hay, pellets and water going: a chinchilla is the least able of the small pets to cope with sugar and fat, so a plate of scraps is the one to avoid rather than a treat. Watch the droppings and ring the vet if it is hunched, not eating, or loose for more than a day.\"],[\"bird\",\"Clear the plate away and give it its own food and water, then watch it: a budgie or a parrot that has had plain bread or veg is usually fine, but anything salty, sugary, fatty or fried, and anything with avocado, chocolate, onion or caffeine in it, is a vet call today. A bird that sits fluffed up, stops eating or has loose droppings needs the vet rather than a wait-and-see, because a bird hides illness until it is very ill.\"]]}")?;
