let __v_2156 = Value::from("Get him out of the car and into the shade now: a car in the sun passes 40C inside within ten minutes, even with a window down, and a dog can only cool himself by panting, so he goes downhill fast. Wet his coat, belly and paws with cool - not iced - water, put him in front of a fan or the car air conditioning, and offer small sips of water. Ring the vet on the way: if he is panting hard, drooling, wobbly, vomiting or limp he needs to be seen, and if he is shut in and in distress ring 999, because the police can break the window. Never leave a dog in a parked car for any length of time on a warm day, and not at all from late spring to early autumn.");
frame.store("_DOG_CAR_FIRST_AID", __v_2156.clone())?;
let __v_2157 = Value::from("Not on a warm day, and not for more than a few minutes at any time of year: a car in the sun passes 40C inside within ten minutes even with a window down. On a cool morning park in the shade with the windows down a couple of inches and water for him, and be back in ten minutes - from late spring to early autumn, leave him at home and tie him up outside the shop instead. If he is already in a hot car, get him into the shade and wet his coat, belly and paws with cool water, and ring the vet if he is panting hard, drooling, wobbly or limp; if he is shut in and in distress, ring 999, because the police can break the window.");
frame.store("_DOG_CAR_RULE", __v_2157.clone())?;
