let __v_8279 = Value::from("Kneading is the one thing she never grew out of: a kitten pushes its paws on the mother to get the milk down, and an adult cat keeps the movement because it feels good. The paws have scent glands, so she is also putting her smell on you, and a cat only does it on something she is settled on. Trim her claws or slide a folded blanket under her - pushing her off teaches her nothing, and a little drooling or purring with it is normal.");
frame.store("_KNEAD_REPLY", __v_8279.clone())?;
let __v_8280 = Value::from("That is a compliment: the scent glands are on the head and cheeks, so a head bump is her putting her smell on you and marking you as safe and hers. Cats do it to the people they trust, and usually as a greeting or an ask, so offer a hand at nose height or bump her back gently and most cats take it as an answer.");
frame.store("_HEADBUTT_REPLY", __v_8280.clone())?;
